ase-za[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Host resource diet for parked runners and the notification store[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Parked agent runners and the ACE TUI stop consuming CPU, RSS, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]swap in proportion to on-disk history: runner-slot admission scans [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]only live capacity state, and the notification store stays O(live) [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]via compaction.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]host_resource_diet.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/host_resource_diet.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-za[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-za/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capacity-only artifact scan in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-scan-mode[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-scan-mode: add an additive sase-core scan option that skips [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]done artifact dirs before parsing and returns only running/waiting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]records, exposed through the scan-options wire and sase_core_rs with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Rust tests and the revision-pin bump.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make parked runners cheap[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]slot-poll-diet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capacity-scan-mode[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]slot-poll-diet: switch the runner-slot wait loop to the capacity-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scan, share one scan per poll window host-wide under the existing lock, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and add jittered backoff with a slot-state change signal while [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preserving admission semantics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep notifications.jsonl O(live)[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]notification-compaction[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]notification-compaction: add crash-safe automatic compaction with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retention window to the Rust notification store, archiving old dismissed[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows to a sibling JSONL file with tests and unchanged Python caller [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live verification and perf floors[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify-resource-diet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after slot-poll-diet, notification-compaction[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify-resource-diet: capture after-measurements on the live host, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]perf-floor benches for the capacity scan and notification snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads, and record residual hotspots on the epic bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-za","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-za.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-f4485c321f46859650c23c23a8e3511a","started_at":"2026-09-10T15:46:41.410497+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-za","bbugyi200.athena.sase-za.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-za.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-za.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-za.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-za.land"]}
